From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:18:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pci: describe paired sleep and optional
 handoff link flush

Document two boolean properties of the S8003 H9P controller.
apple,paired-system-sleep marks an ANS controller whose port keeps power
across system sleep and is stopped and restarted together with it.
apple,ans-kexec-link-flush makes a warm handoff consume a stale link-up
status under PERST before the link is stopped.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml     | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
index f9b72ce26..cebf60d8a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
@@ -231,6 +231,17 @@ properties:
       without exposing a root bridge. This is used when an enabled port shares
       PHY state with a firmware-enabled sibling port.
 
+  apple,ans-kexec-link-flush:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Consume stale ANS link status under PERST during warm handoff.
+
+  apple,paired-system-sleep:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The ANS controller is paired with retained-power port reset over system
+      sleep.
+
   interrupt-controller: true
 
   '#interrupt-cells':
